Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:27:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bot Control: click the ground for a copyable x y z

A plain click on the ground in World 3D (no group tool armed) or in
Instance Watch (not on a player marker) opens a small popup with the
point's x y z, selected for Ctrl+C, and buttons that copy it as is, as
"moveto x y z" for a bot panel's text box, or as "go x;y;z" to whisper a
bot in game. Esc or x closes it; the next click replaces it. On the flat
map the height is the leader's (the module finds the ground near it), as
for the group bar's Move. Clipboard API first, then the selected-text copy.

- formatPointText in bot-command-rules; the copied moveto goes back
  through normalizeBotCommand unchanged (test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
